false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:12:49Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "next", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:12:51Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "12.\tOn April 25, 1901, New York Governor Benjamin Odell Jr. signed into law a bill requiring owners of Xs to register with the state. It also mandated that every X bear “the separate initials of the owner’s name placed upon the back thereof in a conspicuous place, the letters forming such initials to be at least three inches in height.” Owners were expected to provide their own identifying letters, and in those early days there were no restrictions on materials, style, or color. One of the first men to comply was a New York lawyer who mounted a pair of blue porcelain Ys bearing his initials on his X. Others used metal house letters on leather or wood, or painted the letters directly on their Xs. ID X (6 points) and Y (9 points). ‎", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:13:01Z", "username": "Abhishek Saluja", "text": "Cars", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:13:01Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Cars", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:13:03Z", "username": "Abhishek Saluja", "text": "License", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:13:04Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "License", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:13:06Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "Plate", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-25T16:13:06Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "License plates", "role": "attempt", "is_c